  m_Text: 'HOW TO FLY

    - START / CONTINUE / RESTART live on the mission dock (left rail); the lower-left dock always pauses and plays.

    - CONTROLS drawer - WAVE LAB tab: shape the wave (amplitude, frequency, exaggeration), save it into four slots, replay it at the point you are observing.

    - ET tab: select station D1/D2/D3, toggle its optical detail and read the LF/HF channel readout.

    - Desktop Enter advances the story; VR input is unchanged.


    WHAT IS REAL / WHAT IS SIMPLIFIED

    - Waves are emitted at merger and travel outward causally at a chosen visualization speed - the causality is real, the speed is not (real gravitational waves move at light speed).

    - A real binary radiates through inspiral too; this demo only shows the post-merger wave for teaching.

    - Strain shown here is ~0.5; real detector strain is ~1e-21. The laser markers are slowed enormously.

    - Michelson principle is real: split -> different arm lengths -> recombine at the splitter -> dark-port intensity.

    - The ET triangle (3 stations, 60-degree arms, a nested LF/HF pair per station) shows the 2020 concept baseline - not final site geometry; drawn at 12 m where the real arms are ~10 km. LF/HF share one qualitative strain - no separate noise curves.

    - NOT simulated: Fabry-Perot build-up, recycling mirrors, suspensions or any noise sources.

    - The spacetime ''sheet'' is a 2D embedding analogy - not a material surface and not a solution of Einstein''s equations.

    - Riding the wave is a viewpoint, not a relativistic frame.'
